The plate is a square-ish side plate of roughly 22 cm. It holds about 7 pieces of cooked potato or possibly turnip, each around 3–4 cm. A piece of that size weighs about 15–20 g, so the total is roughly 110 g.

Roasted potato runs about 1.0–1.5 kcal/g. These pieces look pan-fried, but the food could also be daikon, which has far fewer calories. Taking the potato reading with a little added oil, I estimate about 130 kcal.

